Size pages' WebGL context budget from the host's renderer.

The cap of live page contexts was fixed at three, the smallest any browser
allows. It now comes from the engine, which derives it from the host's
renderer when it creates its own context (or takes the embedder's setting):
far more pages fit on a GPU, and the engine's context still never becomes the
oldest one past the browser's cap.

diff --git a/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/emscripten/GraphicsContextGLEmscripten.cpp b/Source/WebCore/platform/graphics/emscripten/GraphicsContextGLEmscripten.cpp
